WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
A figure in a top hat stands
alone on a page of printed text.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.750
He's mean.

3
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:06.990
He's cold.

4
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.760
He's "solitary as an oyster".

5
00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:11.480
The camera pulls back.

6
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:16.070
His outline starts to flicker, as
if it isn't drawn in lines at all.

7
00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.500
So is Scrooge a person?

8
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.510
And why would an examiner
care about the answer?

9
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:24.930
In this mission, you'll map
everything we're told about Scrooge,

10
00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.360
from his name to his childhood.

11
00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.580
Should you write about his
feelings, as if you knew him?

12
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.980
You'll test two ways of talking about him,

13
00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.290
and see which one examiners reward.

14
00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.970
And you'll follow Scrooge
from Stave 1 to Stave 5,

15
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:40.920
simile by simile.

16
00:00:40.970 --> 00:00:45.580
Your mission: explain why examiners
care whether Scrooge is a person.
